@first-name: Nat
@last-name: Condit-Schultz
@affiliation: Georgia Tech School of Music, Computational and Cognitive Musicology Lab
@city: Atlanta
@country: Canada
@bio:

	Nat Condit-Schultz is a musician, composer, and scientist,
	specializing in the statistical modeling of musical
	structure. Nat completed his doctorate in music theory and
	cognition at Ohio State University, advised by David Huron,
	and currently serves as Director of the Graduate Program
	for the Georgia Institute of Technology’s School of
	Music, where he also conducts and advises research as co-PI
	of the <a href="https://ccml.gtcmt.gatech.edu/">Computational and Cognitive Musicology Lab</a>.

@@END: BIO